SUMMARY:Toronto Fringe Festival:  Tango After Midnight ($19)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nCan you join us at ***FRINGE***--early
  July??\n\nWe'll attend 'just' two performances.\n\n$19 tickets. Details b
 elow.\n\n### June 30-July 12\, 2026\n\nWelcome to the **38th annual Toront
 o Fringe Festival**\, Toronto's place for indie theatre and performance. W
 ith [123 shows](https://fringetoronto.com/fringe/shows) at [27 venues](htt
 ps://fringetoronto.com/accessibility/access-at-venues/venues) across the c
 ity!\n\nSunday July 5th (2pm-4pm)\n\n***TANGO After Midnight-- (55 minutes
 )***\n\nAs night falls\, a new dance emerges...\n\nPointeTango—winner of
  the Toronto Fringe Patrons’ Pick and the B Street Collaborative Dance A
 ward—ignites the stage with a striking fusion of pointe shoes and stilet
 tos. This electrifying production blends Argentine tango with classical ba
 llet\, interwoven with cinematic projections filmed on location in Buenos 
 Aires.\n\nFast-paced and visually arresting\, the work features innovative
  lighting and sound design\, alongside world-class performers and 2025 Can
 adian Tango Champions Erin Scott-Kafadar and Alexander Richardson.\n\n**A 
 15-time Fringe Award–winning company.**\n\n★★★★★ “Breathtaki
 ng artistry” –Winnipeg Free Press\n★★★★★ “They dance as on
 e body\, with grace and precision” –Monday Magazine\n\n**Ticket link h
 ere**--(our group will attend Sunday July 5th)\n\nhttps://fringetoronto.co
 m/fringe/show/tango-after-midnight\n\nDon't delay--Fringe tickets sell out
  quickly! $19 per person.
