SUMMARY:Toronto Fringe Festival:  Night Journey ($19)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nCan you join us at ***FRINGE***--early
  July??\n\nWe'll attend 'just' two performances.\n\n$19 tickets. Details b
 elow.\n\n\\#\\#\\# June 30\\-July 12\\\, 2026\n\nWelcome to the **38th ann
 ual Toronto Fringe Festival**\, Toronto's place for indie theatre and perf
 ormance. With [123 shows](https://fringetoronto.com/fringe/shows) at [27 v
 enues](https://fringetoronto.com/accessibility/access-at-venues/venues) ac
 ross the city!\n\nTuesday July 7th (7pm-9pm) ***At the Arts & Letters Club
 !***\n\n**Night Journey-- (80 minutes)**\n\nThis original\, full-length pl
 ay explores the dynamics among five strangers in a college night class stu
 dying the Greek epic\, The Odyssey. Each is broken in his or her own way\;
  all are in quest of a better life. This challenging work of theatre is br
 ought fully to life by Night Journey's exceptional cast of actors.\n\n**Pe
 rformances are being held at the beautiful Arts and Letters Club of Toront
 o\, 14 Elm St**. Come early or stay late and enjoy the Club’s lounge or 
 take a tour of our heritage building with its impressive collection of Can
 adian art.\n\n**Ticket link here:** (our group will attend Tuesday July 7t
 h)\n\nhttps://fringetoronto.com/fringe/show/night-journey\n\nDon't delay--
 Fringe tickets sell out quickly! $19 per person.\n\nProducer: Martin Jones
 \, Renée Stein\, Gregory Light\, with the assistance of members of the Ar
 ts and Letters Club **and six talented students from Toronto Metropolitan 
 University’s School of Performance.**\n\nWe must support this!!
