SUMMARY:MONTREAL:  Summer in the City  (ART\, World MUSIC Festival\, FOOD)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nWe've not been on a **summer ART trip*
 * to Montreal in a few years. Long weekend.\n\nWe had previously attended 
 the Montreal Jazz Festival---6 years in a row!\n\nMontreal is home to an i
 ncredible amount of **FESTIVALS.** I cannot keep track as new ones are add
 ed!\n\n**PLEASE READ everything over FIRST--then email me directly your in
 terest.**\n\n**torontoisculture@gmail.com**\n\n*Our Montreal interests*: A
 rt\, architecture\, dance\, film\, food\, music\, opera\, theatre---a mix.
  Each trip is different and unique. We fit a mix of these together each tr
 ip.\n\nMost trips have a combo of about 10 places of interest for us. And 
 lots of walking.\n\n**VERY IMPORTANT**: Please read all the information be
 fore signing up to this trip\, as there is a **non-refundable fee paid up 
 front**.\n\n*Please email me directly before signing up.*\n\n**$125 per pe
 rson trip fee**\n\nThis trip will revolve around **Art\, World Music Festi
 val\, Food**--and will replicate a trip we did in 2018.\n\nWe will attend 
 the **Festival International Nuits d’Afrique** (for the 2nd time). Final
  night showcase concert of 'up and coming' **world music musicians**. Outd
 oors!\n\n* https://www.mtl.org/en/what-to-do/festivals-and-events/festival
 -international-nuits-d-afrique\n* https://www.festivalnuitsdafrique.com/en
 /accueil/\n* https://montrealgazette.com/entertainment_life/dunlevy-13-dai
 ly-picks-for-montreals-39th-nuits-dafrique-music-festival\n\n**For JULY tr
 ip:**\n\n3 nights (Thursday (16th)\, Friday (17th)\, Saturday (18th))\n\nC
 heck your schedules and calendars--and then double check them.\n\n--As wit
 h all my trips\, **YOU are responsible** for your own travel\, insurance\,
  accommodations. I can give you some suggestions. **I AM responsible** for
  organizing everything on the ground while in Montreal.\n\nSchedule\, tour
 s\, reserving tickets\, reservations\, other..\n\nWe ALL meetup in downtow
 n Montreal **about 5pm** on Thursday July 16th--so plan your travel arriva
 l accordingly.\n\nI provide 2 1/2 days of on-the-ground programming: Thurs
 day night\, all day Friday and Saturday. Most return home on Sunday mornin
 g. I do.\n\nFor travel: Bus is about $100\, Train is about $150\, Air is a
 bout $300\, or drive.\n\nI travel on VIA--and stay at Airbnb.\n\nOn this c
 ultural long weekend adventure\, we will focus our attention on FOOD\, Wor
 ld Music Festival\, also 5-6 important **art gallery** visits-meeting with
  gallery owners and artists\, and of course our traditional ***GROUP dinne
 r on last night*!!** We go somewhere new every trip. Budget about **$150 f
 or this.**\n\n\\*\\*This is PEAK summer in Montreal--so **planning ahead (
 offsets)** the cost of my non-refundable fee! Book and reserve now/soon.\n
 \n***FYI:***\n\n* There is no "wrong" place to stay. On previous trips\, A
 irbnb and Hotels seem to be the norm. It's all based on your personal budg
 et. Ideally you are staying close to Place des Arts (within 1km--east\, we
 st\, south)\n* **Budget** another $100 for various tickets/tours\n* Montre
 al is very easy to get around in...excellent Metro system. BUT we walk eve
 rywhere--generally.\n* **There is NON-REFUNDABLE fee to attend my trips\, 
 and is due when you are confirmed. $125 per person**\n\n\\*\\*Each trip is
  unique\, individual\, and never to be repeated! For the culturally curiou
 s! Art enthusiast. Explorers!\n\nOver to you!\n\nCan you join in? Returnin
 g with us again/or first time! The connections people make on these trips-
 -are for life! Priceless. For me also.\n\nPLEASE don't rush to sign-up. Em
 ail me first.\n\nYou're not confirmed until the $125 is paid (via e/transf
 er)--and we have email confirmation between us.\n\nThank you.\n\nGreg\n\nt
 orontoisculture@gmail.com
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/31303
 7574/
